{"id":"81655aa7-0548-477b-9588-807f0214cb5f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0e62ebda0c33ff23","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/hidden-timers.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a9e7576a3acd41d77eccaa00c3696b44e5be878a","start":1,"end":21},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","LONG_MS","=","1000"]},"context":{"after":"e03241e9a1ad291a"}},"payload":{"text":"A hidden tab's timers, kept. A browser holds back a hidden page's timers — Chrome's budget for a background page's\nCPU, and Brave's with it: once a page has spent it (this one, loading a repository), a 10 s setTimeout hadn't fired\nafter 91 s, and an idle hidden page's 1 s interval ran 7 times in 30 s (2026-10-31) — while the page still handles\nits messages at once, and a worker's timers keep time. An agent drives the editor while nobody looks at its tab, and\nthen whatever waits on a timer stops: logs' flush, runs' ends, requests' timeouts. So in each realm on the page's\nthread (main.tsx's two, the workbench's), a timer set while the tab is hidden — or one of LONG_MS or more, which may\noutlast the tab being shown — is a worker's, its firing a message the realm handles. A short one while the tab is\nshown, most of them, is the realm's own.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:12.255Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:12.255Z"}
{"id":"85a7bcc2-3fdb-4016-9312-e499e04ed531","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e03241e9a1ad291a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/hidden-timers.ts","baseline":{"blob":"123f9f6ca615b5e00a836bc5414a79caa176e28f","start":1013,"end":1043},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","FIRST_ID","=","1_000_000_000"]},"context":{"before":"0e62ebda0c33ff23","after":"2a02980fcb2d97cb"}},"payload":{"text":"The worker's timers' ids, apart from the realm's own (which count up from 1).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:10.645Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:10.645Z"}
{"id":"cfb9b999-1fb2-40d2-8eb1-98e204edee59","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"d87167c575f60d3f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/hidden-timers.ts","baseline":{"blob":"e0c3e6afa104de3184a049111328ecc21a42790a","start":3302,"end":3508},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","typeof","handler","!==","\"","function","\"","||","(","realm",".","document","?.","hidden","!==","true","&&","delay","<","LONG_MS",")",")","{","return","(","repeat","?","own",".","setInterval",":","own",".","setTimeout",")","(","handler","as","Callback",",","ms",",","...","args",")","as","unknown","as","number",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"facf349fa44167ca","after":"c40b0b5e2e7751a9"}},"payload":{"text":"(a string to evaluate, or a short timer while the tab is shown: the realm's own)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:07.430Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:07.430Z"}
{"id":"d116310c-ba27-4f23-a16e-52442f0667f3","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0e62ebda0c33ff23","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/hidden-timers.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1463f379ca8cb3f1f4e668cd2e2241aef7d17d61","start":882,"end":902},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","LONG_MS","=","1000"]},"context":{"after":"e03241e9a1ad291a"}},"payload":{"text":"A timer this long or longer is a worker's however the tab is: the tab can be hidden before it's due.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:11.455Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:11.455Z"}
